		<FBProgram name="Info">
			<STSource>(*

Works with HMI's 

Every screen is the same. the only differents is his IP-Adress
(all works on the Ip-Adress)
only 1 screen can be active, and have the controls

in every screens are 5 actions running...
(it is possible to put them all 1 one action,in vijeo, but for debugging is this more readable )


There is one struct variable 


InOut SwitchScreen


switchScreen is a Array of struct ScreenSwitch 


struct ScreenSwitch +
		    + ConnectedScreen  string(16);  IP Adress HMI
		    + ActiveScreen     int       ;  Number of active screen
		    + SwitchScreenCnt  int       ;  By take over  shows the countdown counter on the screens
		    + Buttons		struct(ScreenSwitchButtons) +
								    + BtnYes			bit
								    + BtnNo			bit	
								    + BtnWantControl		bit
								    + OtherScreenWantControl	bit
								    + ThisScreenIaAlive		bit

*)

(* 
2020-10-27 asw
make 4 default ipadress inputs.
if there is a Ip adress on the input.. then if a found IP adress is the same as the ip adress at the input, the screen always get that number
*)

(*
2020-10-28 asw
Block take over , on the active screen you can block the take over on the other screens..
If Input 'PassWord' is true, the button  'Block take over' is enabled. so if it always high, they always can control this function
if you use a password bit, the need to give a good password first.
if they press the button while it is blocked, output 'PressedWhileBlocked' is one cyclus High, so you can use it for a warning in the screen,
or open the password popup.
*)

(*
2021-03-15
little change, that the array pointer needs tobe bigger as 0 , so we don't get %s20 alarms anymore
*)

(* action in the hmi screens (in all screens they are the same, it all works on the different IP-Adress
First script checks in the PLC if his IP-Adress is already in the list
If it not, it search for a empty spot, and put his IP-adress there

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
action 1 
periodic , 0,5 sec

ScreenOnCounter=ScreenOnCounter + 1


script in HMI

			//  make intern variables
			int Count=0;
			String IpAdress;
			int alreadyInList;
			int ScreenOnCount;

			IpAdress="";

			ScreenOnCount=ScreenOnCounter.getIntValue();

			if (ScreenOnCount&gt;10)
			{

			// get ip adress from this HMI
			IpAdress=Sys.getInfoString(IP_ADDRESS_1);

			alreadyInList=0;
			// Check is this Ip-Adress already is in the list in the PLC
			while (Count&lt;4)
			{
			  if (ScreenChange.SwitchScreen[Count].ConnectedScreen.getStringValue().compareTo(IpAdress) == 0)
			  {
			  alreadyInList=1;	
			  return; // &lt;-Yes, so exit script
			  };
			 Count++;
			  };
  
			Count=0;

			// No, Ip-Adress is not in the list
			// search a empt place, and copy Ip-Adres in list
			if (alreadyInList==0){
			  while (Count&lt;4)
			  {
			    if (ScreenChange.SwitchScreen[Count].ConnectedScreen.getStringValue().compareTo("") == 0)
			    {
			      ScreenChange.SwitchScreen[Count].ConnectedScreen.write(IpAdress);
			      return;
			    };
			    Count++;  
			    };
			   };
			 };


---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
action 2 
periodic , 0,1 sec
script in HMI


			int Cnt=0;
			String IpAdress;


			IpAdress="";

			IpAdress=Sys.getInfoString(IP_ADDRESS_1);


			// check if this hmi already in the list, and what is his number
			while (Cnt&lt;4)
			{
			  if (ScreenChange.SwitchScreen[Cnt].ConnectedScreen.getStringValue().compareTo(IpAdress) == 0)
			    {
			    ScreenChange.ScreenNumber.write(Cnt); // &lt;- put number of this screen in the list 
			    };
			  Cnt++;
			};
  

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
action 3 
periodic , 0,1 sec
script in HMI


			int ScreenNumber=0;
			int thisScreenActive=0;

			// copy bits from list in the plc to internal bits in the screen
			// this because I want all the screens the same

			// Get screennumber from list in the PLC
			ScreenNumber = ScreenChange.ScreenNumber.getIntValue();

			// copy status internal bit ThisScreenActive from list in the PLC
			thisScreenActive = ScreenChange.SwitchScreen[ScreenNumber].ActiveScreen.getIntValue();

			// copy intern bit ScreenIsAlve to list in the PLC
			if (thisScreenActive  == 1)
			{
			    ScreenChange.ScreenIsActive.write(1);
			}
			else
			{
			    ScreenChange.ScreenIsActive.write(0);
			};
		
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
action 4
periodic , 0,5 sec
script in HMI

			int ScreenNumber;

			// get number from this screen
			ScreenNumber = ScreenChange.ScreenNumber.getIntValue();

			// set alive bit in this screen
			// PLc reset this bit
			// If bit stays low, screen is not alive
			ScreenChange.SwitchScreen[ScreenChange.ScreenNumber.getIntValue()].buttons.ThisScreenIsAlive.write(1);

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Word  gebruikt in :

190117 FUJIAN DN455 01&amp;02
060000 VAMO NACC NEWYORKER 05034

250081 NACC XL288 &amp; NACC XL289
*)

(* ************************************************************************** *)
(* ************  SwitchScreens  -  Function Block Documentation  ************ *)
(* ************************************************************************** *)
(*                                                                            *)
(*   FB Name                   : SwitchScreens                                *)
(*   Version                   : 1.46                                         *)
(*   Platform                  : Schneider Control Expert V14.1               *)
(*   HMI                       : Vijeo Designer                               *)
(*   Max screens               : 4                                            *)
(*   Author                    : ASW                                          *)
(*   Updated                   : 2026                                         *)
(*                                                                            *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*   1. PURPOSE                                                               *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* This FB manages multiple identical HMI panels connected to one PLC.        *)
(* Only ONE panel is active at a time and may send operator commands.         *)
(* All other panels are view-only monitors.                                   *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Key features:                                                              *)
(*   - All panels run the SAME Vijeo application - no separate app per        *)
(*     location                                                               *)
(*   - Panel identity is based on IP address - read at runtime by HMI script  *)
(*   - Panels self-register in the PLC array on startup - no manual config    *)
(*     needed                                                                 *)
(*   - Take-over: any panel can request control, active panel can allow or    *)
(*     deny                                                                   *)
(*   - Automatic take-over if active panel does not respond within countdown  *)
(*   - Block take-over: active panel can lock out requests (password          *)
(*     protected)                                                             *)
(*   - Alive monitoring: offline panels are automatically removed from the    *)
(*     list                                                                   *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*   2. BACKGROUND                                                            *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Originally all panels were parallel - any panel could operate at any time. *)
(* This caused confusion when two operators worked simultaneously.            *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* First fix: separate Vijeo app per location (bridge/controlroom/mess).      *)
(* Problem: every change had to be made in 3 projects. Easy to forget one.    *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Solution: one application for all panels, identity via IP address.         *)
(* The PLC handles all switching logic. HMI scripts handle registration.      *)
(* A change to any screen element is made ONCE and applies to all panels.     *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*   3. DATA STRUCTURES                                                       *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* InOut: SwitchScreenInOut[1..4] OF ScreenSwitch                             *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* ScreenSwitch struct:                                                       *)
(*     ConnectedScreen         : STRING[16] - IP address, written by HMI      *)
(*                               Script 1                                     *)
(*     ActiveScreen            : INT - 1=this panel active, 0=view only       *)
(*     SwitchScreenCnt         : INT - countdown seconds during take-over     *)
(*     Buttons                 : ScreenSwitchButtons - bit-packed word (see   *)
(*                               below)                                       *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* ScreenSwitchButtons - bit layout:                                          *)
(*     Bit  0 BtnYes       HMI-&gt;PLC          active panel confirms take-over  *)
(*     Bit  1 BtnNo        HMI-&gt;PLC          active panel denies take-over    *)
(*     Bit  2 BtnWantCtrl  HMI-&gt;PLC          view-only panel requests control *)
(*     Bit  3 OtherWants   PLC-&gt;HMI          show take-over popup on ALL      *)
(*                                           panels                           *)
(*     Bit  4 BtnBlock     HMI-&gt;PLC          active panel toggles block flag  *)
(*     Bit  5 BlockGate    PLC-&gt;HMI          block button enabled (password   *)
(*                                           gate)                            *)
(*     Bit  6 PressBlocked  HMI-&gt;PLC          pressed take-over while blocked *)
(*                                            (1-shot)                        *)
(*     Bit  7 IsBlocked    PLC-&gt;HMI          broadcast - take-over is         *)
(*                                           currently blocked                *)
(*     Bit  8 BtnMirror    HMI-&gt;PLC          toggle mirror/orientation        *)
(*                                           (momentary)                      *)
(*     Bit  9 MirrorState  PLC-&gt;HMI          current mirror state of this     *)
(*                                           panel                            *)
(*     Bit 10-14 UserBits  both              free bits - used by              *)
(*                                           SwitchScreenMemmory FB           *)
(*     Bit 15 Alive        HMI-&gt;PLC          heartbeat, set every 0.5s by     *)
(*                                           Script 4                         *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*   4. INPUTS                                                                *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*                                                                            *)
(*     Reset                   : BOOL - rising edge clears entire panel list  *)
(*     DefaultIpNo1            : STRING - this IP address always at array     *)
(*                               position 1                                   *)
(*     DefaultIpNo2            : STRING - this IP address always at array     *)
(*                               position 2                                   *)
(*     DefaultIpNo3            : STRING - this IP address always at array     *)
(*                               position 3                                   *)
(*     DefaultIpNo4            : STRING - this IP address always at array     *)
(*                               position 4                                   *)
(*     PassWordActive          : BOOL - enables block button on active panel  *)
(*     AutoSwitchTime          : INT - take-over countdown in seconds         *)
(*                               (default 5)                                  *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*   5. OUTPUTS                                                               *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*                                                                            *)
(*     ScreenActive            : INT - index of active panel (0=none)         *)
(*     WantsControl            : INT - index of panel requesting take-over    *)
(*     PressedWhileBlocked     : BOOL - 1-shot: take-over pressed while       *)
(*                               blocked                                      *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*   6. PROGRAM SECTIONS (execution order)                                    *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*                                                                            *)
(*     Info                    : This documentation - not executed            *)
(*     ResetData               : Dedup IPs, heartbeat reset, alive counters,  *)
(*                               remove offline                               *)
(*     SchermWissel            : Core take-over: countdown, Yes/No, auto      *)
(*                               take-over                                    *)
(*     DefaultIpPlace          : Sort panels to fixed positions via DefaultIp *)
(*                               inputs                                       *)
(*     PressWhileBlocked       : Set PressedWhileBlocked output for one scan  *)
(*                               cycle                                        *)
(*     ReleaseBlocked          : Gate block button via PassWordActive input   *)
(*     BlockedToOtherScreens   : Broadcast TakeOverIsBlocked to all connected *)
(*                               panels                                       *)
(*     SomethingWrong          : Watchdog: stuck bits, BtnYes+BtnNo both high *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*   7. TAKE-OVER PROCEDURE                                                   *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Example: Panel 2 (view-only) wants control from Panel 1 (active).          *)
(*                                                                            *)
(*     Step 1              Panel 2           sets BtnWantControl (bit 2)      *)
(*     Step 2              PLC               ChangeScreen=TRUE,               *)
(*                                           WantsControl=2,                  *)
(*                                           Counter=AutoSwitchTime           *)
(*     Step 3              PLC               OtherScreenWantsControl set on   *)
(*                                           ALL panels - popup               *)
(*     Step 4a             Panel 1 YES       Panel 2 becomes active           *)
(*                                           immediately                      *)
(*     Step 4b             Panel 1 NO        take-over rejected, all flags    *)
(*                                           reset                            *)
(*     Step 4c             No reaction       after countdown Panel 2 becomes  *)
(*                                           active automatically             *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Step 4c is intentional: unattended active panel -&gt; requesting panel gets   *)
(* control automatically without anyone going back to the active screen.      *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*   8. BLOCK TAKE-OVER                                                       *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Active panel can block all take-over requests. Password protected.         *)
(* EMERGENCY feature only - in normal daily operation block is OFF.           *)
(*                                                                            *)
(*   - TakeOverIsBlocked (bit 7) set on all connected panels when blocked     *)
(*   - View-only panels show 'Take over is blocked' warning                   *)
(*   - PressedWhileBlocked output pulses if panel tries anyway                *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* To unblock: physically go to active panel, enter password, press button.   *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*   9. SCREEN-ALIVE MONITORING                                               *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*                                                                            *)
(*     HMI Script 4        every 500ms       sets bit 15 (ThisScreenIsAlive)  *)
(*                                           to 1                             *)
(*     PLC                 every 1s          resets all alive bits (%S6       *)
(*                                           rising edge)                     *)
(*     AliveCounter        starts at 150     decrements each scan, resets on  *)
(*                                           rising edge                      *)
(*     Timeout             ~1.5 seconds      counter reaches 0 -&gt; panel       *)
(*                                           removed from list                *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*   10. HMI SCRIPTS (Vijeo Designer) - identical on all panels               *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* HMI internal vars (INT): ScreenOnCounter, ScreenNumber, ScreenIsActive     *)
(* PLC variable in scripts : ScreenChange  (= SwitchScreenInOut array)        *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -- Script 1: Register IP address (periodic 0.5s) --                        *)
(*     int Count=0;                                                           *)
(*     String IpAddress=Sys.getInfoString(IP_ADDRESS_1);                      *)
(*     if (ScreenOnCounter.getIntValue() &gt; 10) {                              *)
(*       while (Count&lt;4) {                                                    *)
(*         if (ScreenChange.SwitchScreen[Count].ConnectedScreen               *)
(*               .getStringValue().compareTo(IpAddress)==0) { return; }       *)
(*         Count++; }                                                         *)
(*       Count=0;                                                             *)
(*       while (Count&lt;4) {                                                    *)
(*         if (ScreenChange.SwitchScreen[Count].ConnectedScreen               *)
(*               .getStringValue().compareTo("")==0) {                        *)
(*       ScreenChange.SwitchScreen[Count].ConnectedScreen.write(IpAddress);   *)
(*           return; }                                                        *)
(*         Count++; } }                                                       *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -- Script 2: Find own screen number (periodic 0.1s) --                     *)
(*     int Cnt=0; String IpAddress=Sys.getInfoString(IP_ADDRESS_1);           *)
(*     while (Cnt&lt;4) {                                                        *)
(*       if (ScreenChange.SwitchScreen[Cnt].ConnectedScreen                   *)
(*             .getStringValue().compareTo(IpAddress)==0)                     *)
(*         { ScreenChange.ScreenNumber.write(Cnt); }                          *)
(*       Cnt++; }                                                             *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -- Script 3: Copy active status (periodic 0.1s) --                         *)
(*     int n=ScreenChange.ScreenNumber.getIntValue();                         *)
(*     int a=ScreenChange.SwitchScreen[n].ActiveScreen.getIntValue();         *)
(*     ScreenChange.ScreenIsActive.write(a==1 ? 1 : 0);                       *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -- Script 4: Heartbeat (periodic 0.5s) --                                  *)
(*     int n=ScreenChange.ScreenNumber.getIntValue();                         *)
(*     ScreenChange.SwitchScreen[n].buttons.ThisScreenIsAlive.write(1);       *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*   11. SCREENISACTIVE - THE UNIVERSAL INTERLOCK                             *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* ScreenIsActive is a local HMI variable set by Script 3.                    *)
(* Set this as the ENABLE condition on every operator control in Vijeo.       *)
(* Vijeo automatically greys out and disables controls when = 0.              *)
(*                                                                            *)
(*     ALWAYS interlock                      start/stop, setpoints, valve     *)
(*                                           controls, mode selection         *)
(*     NEVER interlock                       page navigation, Take over       *)
(*                                           button, display objects          *)
(*     OPTIONAL                              alarm reset (your choice per     *)
(*                                           project)                         *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*   12. THIRD-PARTY INTEGRATION - Kongsberg / Praxis / Modbus / OPC          *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Any system can participate. Only 4 things needed:                          *)
(*                                                                            *)
(*     1. REGISTER         once at start     write own ID to                  *)
(*                                    SwitchScreenInOut[n].ConnectedScreen    *)
(*     2. POLL             every 100ms       read ActiveScreen: 1=active      *)
(*                                           (on), 0=view only (off)          *)
(*     3. HEARTBEAT        every 500ms       write bit 15 of Buttons.Wrd to 1 *)
(*     4. TAKE-OVER        on request        write bit 2 (BtnWantControl)     *)
(*                                           once to request                  *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Slot: agree fixed slot with installer OR find first empty slot at startup. *)
(* Modbus: STRING[16] = 9 holding registers. Ask installer for address map.   *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*   13. COMPANION FB: SwitchScreenMemmory                                    *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* See SwitchScreenMemmory FB for per-screen persistent settings.             *)
(* Uses bits 9-14 of Buttons.Wrd as memory bits per IP address.               *)
(* Typical use: PS/SB orientation, mirror view, language, local preferences.  *)
(* Declare MemoryWrd[1..4] OF WORD as RETAIN.                                 *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*   14. NOTES FOR FUTURE MAINTAINERS                                         *)
(* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- *)
(*                                                                            *)
(*   - Declare SwitchScreenInOut as RETAIN - must survive PLC power cycle     *)
(*   - AutoSwitchTime=15s typical maritime (bridge unattended scenario)       *)
(*   - secPuls uses %S6 (1Hz system bit) - no extra timer FB needed           *)
(*   - IS_PAR_CON guards DefaultIp inputs - unconnected inputs are safe       *)
(*   - SomethingWrong clears stuck OtherScreenWantsControl after 500 scans    *)
(*   - First panel auto-becomes active on PLC start (NoScreenHasControl       *)
(*     logic)                                                                 *)
(*   - Block is behind password - normal daily use does NOT use block         *)
(*                                                                            *)
</STSource>
		</FBProgram>
		<FBProgram name="ResetData">
			<STSource>
(* copy Input Reset to eBool for egde detection*)
tmpReset:=Reset;

(* auxiliary bit SameIp , true if there is 2x the same Ip adress in the list *)
SameIp:=false;

(* Compare all screen IP addresses with each other, see if there are the same IP addresses in the list *)
for cnt:=1 to 4 do
	for cnt2:=1 to 4 do
		if SwitchScreenInOut[cnt].ConnectedScreen&lt;&gt;'' and SwitchScreenInOut[cnt2].ConnectedScreen&lt;&gt;'' and cnt2&gt;cnt then
			if SwitchScreenInOut[cnt].ConnectedScreen=SwitchScreenInOut[cnt2].ConnectedScreen then
				SwitchScreenInOut[cnt2].ConnectedScreen:='';
			end_if;
		end_if;
	end_for;
end_for;

(* put all Alive toggle bits low *)
if re(secPuls) then
	for cnt:=1 to 4 do
		SwitchScreenInOut[cnt].Buttons.ThisScreenIsAlive:=0;
	end_for;
end_if;

(* check if a screen does not answer anymore *)
LostAScreen:=false;
lostScreenNbr:=0;
for cnt:=1 to 4 do 

	ScreenIsAlive[cnt]:=SwitchScreenInOut[cnt].Buttons.ThisScreenIsAlive;
	
	if re(ScreenIsAlive[cnt]) then
		AliveCounter[cnt]:=150;
	end_if;

	if AliveCounter[cnt]&gt;0 then
		AliveCounter[cnt]:=AliveCounter[cnt]-1;
	end_if;

	if AliveCounter[cnt]=0 and PreAliveCounter[cnt]&gt;0 then	
		SwitchScreenInOut[cnt].ActiveScreen:=0;
		LostAScreen:=true;
		lostScreenNbr:=cnt;
	end_if;

	PreAliveCounter[cnt]:=AliveCounter[cnt];

end_for;

if LostAScreen and lostScreenNbr&gt;0 then
	SwitchScreenInOut[lostScreenNbr].ConnectedScreen:='';
	SwitchScreenInOut[lostScreenNbr].Buttons.Wrd:=0;
end_if;

(* clear list with Ip Adressen *)
if re(tmpReset) or SameIp  then
	for cnt:=1 to 4 do
		SwitchScreenInOut[cnt].ConnectedScreen:='';
		SwitchScreenInOut[lostScreenNbr].Buttons.Wrd:=0;
	end_for;
end_if;

(* For debuggen *)
temp1:=AliveCounter[1]; temp5:=ScreenIsAlive[1];temp9:=SwitchScreenInOut[1].Buttons.ThisScreenIsAlive;
temp2:=AliveCounter[2]; temp6:=ScreenIsAlive[2];temp10:=SwitchScreenInOut[2].Buttons.ThisScreenIsAlive;
temp3:=AliveCounter[3]; temp7:=ScreenIsAlive[3];temp11:=SwitchScreenInOut[3].Buttons.ThisScreenIsAlive;
temp4:=AliveCounter[4]; temp8:=ScreenIsAlive[4];temp12:=SwitchScreenInOut[4].Buttons.ThisScreenIsAlive;
</STSource>
		</FBProgram>
		<FBProgram name="SchermWissel">
			<STSource>
(* if there is a value in input AutoSwitchTime, use that value, else use a default value *)

if IS_PAR_CON (INP := AutoSwitchTime) then
	SwitchTime:=AutoSwitchTime;
else
	SwitchTime:=5;
End_if;

(* auxiliary bit secPuls for egde detection *)
secPuls:=%s6;

(*------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*)
NoScreenHasControl:=True;
for ScreenNumber:=1 to 4 do

       (* check which HMI is now in control *)
	if SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].ActiveScreen=1 then
		ScreenActive:=ScreenNumber;
		NoScreenHasControl:=False;
	end_if;

	(* check whether the TakeOver button is pressed somewhere*) 
  	if SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].Buttons.BtnWantControl=1 and SwitchCounter&lt;1 then
		ChangeScreen:=true;
		SwitchCounter:=SwitchTime;
		WantsControl:=ScreenNumber;                                 (*Number HMI that wants Control*)
		SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].Buttons.BtnWantControl:=false;
	end_if;
end_for;

(*------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*)
(* No Hmi screen Active, so make HMI one active *)
if NoScreenHasControl=True then
	for ScreenNumber:=1 to 4 do
		if SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].ConnectedScreen&lt;&gt;'' then
			SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].ActiveScreen:=1;
			exit;
		end_if;
	end_for;
end_if;

(*------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*)
(* They pushed NO, taking over is not allowed  *)
if ScreenActive&gt;0 then
	if SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].Buttons.BtnNo and ScreenActive&gt;0 then
	
		SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].SwitchScreenCnt:=0;
		SwitchScreenInOut[WantsControl].SwitchScreenCnt:=0;
	
		ChangeScreen:=false;
		SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].Buttons.OtherScreenWantsControl:=False;
		SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].Buttons.BtnNo:=false;
		SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].Buttons.BtnYes:=false;
		SwitchCounter:=0;
	end_if;
end_if;

(*------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*)
(* they pushed Yes , Take over allowed *)
if ScreenActive&gt;0 then
	if SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].Buttons.BtnYes then
		(*make all screens not active*)
		for ScreenNumber:=1 to 4 do
			SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].ActiveScreen:=0;
		end_for;

		(* make new screen active*)
		SwitchScreenInOut[WantsControl].ActiveScreen:=1;


		(* reset other screens *)
		SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].SwitchScreenCnt:=0;
		SwitchScreenInOut[WantsControl].SwitchScreenCnt:=0;
	
		ChangeScreen:=false;
		SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].Buttons.OtherScreenWantsControl:=False;
		SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].Buttons.BtnNo:=false;
		SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].Buttons.BtnYes:=false;
		SwitchCounter:=0;
	end_if;
end_if;

(*------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*)
(* Time is over, and they not pushed NO, so Take Over is allowed*)
if ChangeScreen and SwitchCounter&lt;1 then
	(*make all screens not active*)
	for ScreenNumber:=1 to 4 do
		SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].ActiveScreen:=0;
	end_for;

	(* make new screen active *)
	SwitchScreenInOut[WantsControl].ActiveScreen:=1;


	(* reset other screens *)
	SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].SwitchScreenCnt:=0;
	SwitchScreenInOut[WantsControl].SwitchScreenCnt:=0;
	
	ChangeScreen:=false;
	SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].Buttons.OtherScreenWantsControl:=False;
	SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].Buttons.BtnNo:=false;
	SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].Buttons.BtnYes:=false;
	SwitchCounter:=0;
end_if;

(*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*)
(* reset all counters *)

for ScreenNumber:=1 to 4 do
	SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].SwitchScreenCnt:=0;
end_for;

(*------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*)
if ChangeScreen and ScreenActive&gt;0 and WantsControl&gt;0 then
	(* show allow to take over question on active screen*)
 	SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].Buttons.OtherScreenWantsControl:=true;

	(* show on active screen, and the screen that wants to take over the countdown counter *)

	SwitchScreenInOut[WantsControl].SwitchScreenCnt:=SwitchCounter;	
	SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].SwitchScreenCnt:=SwitchCounter;

end_if;

(*------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*)
(* dec switch countdown counter *)
if SwitchCounter&gt;0 then
	if re(secpuls) then
		SwitchCounter:=SwitchCounter-1;
	end_if;
end_if;


for ScreenNumber:=1 to 4 do
	If ChangeScreen=false and SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].SwitchScreenCnt&lt;&gt;0 then
		SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].SwitchScreenCnt:=0;
	end_if;
end_for;
</STSource>
		</FBProgram>
		<FBProgram name="DefaultIpPlace">
			<STSource>
if IS_PAR_CON (INP := DefaultIpNo1) then

	DefaultIp1Inlist:=false;
	Found1AtPlace:=0;

	(* Compare all screen IP addresses with DefaultIp1 *)
	for cnt:=1 to 4 do
		if SwitchScreenInOut[cnt].ConnectedScreen=DefaultIpNo1  then
			DefaultIp1Inlist:=true;
			Found1AtPlace:=Cnt;	
		end_if;
	end_for;
	if DefaultIp1Inlist then
		if Found1AtPlace&lt;&gt;1 then (* not on the wright place, so switch them*)
			tmpSwitchScreenInOut:=SwitchScreenInOut[1]; (* copy info from 1 to a temp place*)
			SwitchScreenInOut[1]:=SwitchScreenInOut[Found1AtPlace]; (* copy found screen to the right place*)
			SwitchScreenInOut[Found1AtPlace]:=tmpSwitchScreenInOut;
		end_if;
	end_if;
end_if;


if IS_PAR_CON (INP := DefaultIpNo2) then

	DefaultIp2Inlist:=false;
	Found2AtPlace:=0;

	(* Compare all screen IP addresses with DefaultIp1 *)
	for cnt:=1 to 4 do
		if SwitchScreenInOut[cnt].ConnectedScreen=DefaultIpNo2  then
			DefaultIp2Inlist:=true;
			Found2AtPlace:=Cnt;	
		end_if;
	end_for;
	if DefaultIp2Inlist then
		if Found2AtPlace&lt;&gt;2 then (* not on the wright place, so switch them*)
			tmpSwitchScreenInOut:=SwitchScreenInOut[2]; (* copy info from 1 to a temp place*)
			SwitchScreenInOut[2]:=SwitchScreenInOut[Found2AtPlace]; (* copy found screen to the right place*)
			SwitchScreenInOut[Found2AtPlace]:=tmpSwitchScreenInOut;
		end_if;
	end_if;
end_if;


if IS_PAR_CON (INP := DefaultIpNo3) then

	DefaultIp3Inlist:=false;
	Found3AtPlace:=0;

	(* Compare all screen IP addresses with DefaultIp1 *)
	for cnt:=1 to 4 do
		if SwitchScreenInOut[cnt].ConnectedScreen=DefaultIpNo3 then
			DefaultIp3Inlist:=true;	
			Found3AtPlace:=Cnt;
		end_if;
	end_for;
	if DefaultIp3Inlist then
		if Found3AtPlace&lt;&gt;3 then (* not on the right place, so switch them*)
			tmpSwitchScreenInOut:=SwitchScreenInOut[3]; (* copy info from 1 to a temp place*)
			SwitchScreenInOut[3]:=SwitchScreenInOut[Found3AtPlace]; (* copy found screen to the right place*)
			SwitchScreenInOut[Found3AtPlace]:=tmpSwitchScreenInOut;
		end_if;
	end_if;
end_if;


if IS_PAR_CON (INP := DefaultIpNo4) then

	DefaultIp4Inlist:=false;
	Found4AtPlace:=0;

	(* Compare all screen IP addresses with DefaultIp1 *)
	for cnt:=1 to 4 do
		if SwitchScreenInOut[cnt].ConnectedScreen=DefaultIpNo4  then
			DefaultIp4Inlist:=true;
			Found4AtPlace:=Cnt;	
		end_if;
	end_for;
	if DefaultIp4Inlist then
		if Found4AtPlace&lt;&gt;4 then (* not on the wright place, so switch them*)
			tmpSwitchScreenInOut:=SwitchScreenInOut[4]; (* copy info from 1 to a temp place*)
			SwitchScreenInOut[4]:=SwitchScreenInOut[Found4AtPlace]; (* copy found screen to the right place*)
			SwitchScreenInOut[Found4AtPlace]:=tmpSwitchScreenInOut;
		end_if;
	end_if;
end_if;

</STSource>
		</FBProgram>
		<FBProgram name="PressWhileBlocked">
			<STSource>

PressedWhileBlocked:=false;

for ScreenNumber:=1 to 4 do
	if SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].Buttons.pressedTakeOverNotAllowedWhileBlocked=1 then
		PressedWhileBlocked:=true;
	end_if;
end_for;


</STSource>
		</FBProgram>
		<FBProgram name="ReleaseBlocked">
			<STSource>

SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].Buttons.BlockBtnTakeOverNotAllowed:=not PassWordActive;
</STSource>
		</FBProgram>
		<FBProgram name="BlockedToOtherScreens">
			<STSource>
	for ScreenNumber:=1 to 4 do
		if SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].ConnectedScreen&lt;&gt;'' then
			SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].Buttons.TakeOverIsBlocked:=false;
		end_if;
	end_for;



if ScreenActive&gt;0 then
	if SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenActive].Buttons.BtnTakeOverNotAllowed=1 then

		for ScreenNumber:=1 to 4 do
			if SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].ConnectedScreen&lt;&gt;'' then
				SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].Buttons.TakeOverIsBlocked:=true;
			end_if;
		end_for;

	end_if;
end_if;
</STSource>
		</FBProgram>
		<FBProgram name="SomethingWrong">
			<STSource>
(* Reset All!!! wen something is wrong *)


(* BtnYes and BtnNo both active?!? *)
for ScreenNumber:=1 to 4 do
	if SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].Buttons.BtnNo and SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].Buttons.BtnYes then
		SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].Buttons.Wrd:=0;
	end_if;
end_for;


(*sometimes bit stays 1 OtherScreenWantsControl??? *)
for ScreenNumber:=1 to 4 do
	if SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].Buttons.OtherScreenWantsControl=1 then
 		otherScreenWantsControl[ScreenNumber]:=True;
	else
 		otherScreenWantsControl[ScreenNumber]:=False;
	end_if;

	if otherScreenWantsControl[ScreenNumber]=True then
		otherscreenControlCounter[ScreenNumber]:=otherscreenControlCounter[ScreenNumber]+1;
	else
		otherscreenControlCounter[ScreenNumber]:=0;
	end_if;

	if otherscreenControlCounter[ScreenNumber]&gt;500 then
		SwitchScreenInOut[ScreenNumber].Buttons.OtherScreenWantsControl:=false;
		otherscreenControlCounter[ScreenNumber]:=0;
	end_if;
end_for;

dummy:=otherScreenWantsControl[1];
dummy:=otherScreenWantsControl[2];
dummy:=otherScreenWantsControl[3];
dummy:=otherScreenWantsControl[4];

dummy0:=otherscreenControlCounter[1];
dummy1:=otherscreenControlCounter[2];
dummy2:=otherscreenControlCounter[3];
dummy3:=otherscreenControlCounter[4];
</STSource>
		</FBProgram>
	</FBSource>
